hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20877","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Harun ibn Ri'ab, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym, from Qabisah ibn al-Mukhariq, he said: I bore a surety burden, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him regarding it, so he said: Stay until charity comes to us, then either we bear it or we help you in it. And he said: Begging is not lawful except for three: A man who bears a surety burden of a people, so he asks regarding it until he fulfills it, then he refrains; and a man struck by a calamity that sweeps away his wealth, so he asks in it until he attains sufficiency of livelihood or support of livelihood, then he refrains; and a man struck by poverty, so he asks until he attains sufficiency of livelihood or support of livelihood, then he refrains; and whatever besides that of begging is unlawful gain, O Qabisah, its taker eats it as unlawful gain."
"20878","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Karimah, a man of Basrah narrated to me, from Qabisah ibn al-Mukhariq, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to me: O Qabisah, what brought you? I said: My age grew old and my bones grew thin, so I came to you to teach me what Allah, mighty and majestic, will benefit me with. He said: O Qabisah, you do not pass by a stone, nor a tree, nor a clod, except it seeks forgiveness for you. O Qabisah, when you pray Fajr, say three times: Glory be to Allah the Mighty and with His praise, you will be healed from blindness, leprosy, and paralysis. O Qabisah, say: O Allah, I ask You from what is with You, and pour upon me from Your bounty, and spread upon me Your mercy, and send down upon me from Your blessings."
"20879","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Hayyan Abu al-Ala, from Qatan ibn Qabisah, from Qabisah ibn al-Mukhariq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Divination by birds, omens, and divination by lines are of jibt."
"20880","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Hayyan, Qatan ibn Qabisah narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Divination by birds, divination by lines, and omens are of jibt. Awf said: Divination is driving birds, and divination by lines is the line drawn in the ground, and jibt, al-Hasan said: It is Satan."
"20881","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq and Zuhayr ibn Amr, he said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended a high spot of a mountain, atop it a stone, and began calling: O sons of Abd Manaf, I am but a warner; my likeness and yours is like a man who saw the enemy and went to warn his people, fearing they would precede him, so he began calling and shouting: O morning calamity."
"20882","Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq and Zuhayr ibn Amr, both said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20883","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah, he said: The sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and prayed two rak'ahs, lengthening the recitation in them, then it cleared, so he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, blessed and exalted, with which He frightens His servants, so when you see that, then pray as the latest prescribed prayer you prayed."
"20884","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah al-Hilali, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was with him in Madinah that day, then he mentioned its meaning."
